WEBVTT

00:11:29.792 --> 00:11:32.205
but I think it's one
of those things in retrospect,

00:11:32.229 --> 00:11:35.205
when you think about some
of the most fulfilling times at work,

00:11:35.229 --> 00:11:37.062
they involve some amount of struggle,

00:11:37.086 --> 00:11:40.303
and I think people felt
really fulfilled by their work.

00:11:40.327 --> 00:11:44.435
Again, I think there was plenty
of peaks of exhaustion,

00:11:44.459 --> 00:11:48.433
but I think they were getting to do
really good work with really good people.

00:11:48.457 --> 00:11:52.639
And I think they felt that sense
of community and excitement.

00:11:52.663 --> 00:11:54.377
AG: The juxtaposition of excitement

00:11:54.401 --> 00:11:56.546
and exhaustion is fascinating to me,

00:11:56.570 --> 00:11:58.501
it reminds me of some research

00:11:58.525 --> 00:12:00.529
on what's called the passion tax,